      "message": "fix(multiaxis): Rotary Flow refuses a crossing between any two guides\n\nThe band loop's meet law read only adjacent guide pairs. A guide that\ncrossed a guide two or more places away in the pick was machined, and\nthe bands of the two adjacent pairs folded through the same ground.\n\nA new law (rotary_flow_cross::refuse_crossed_set) reads every\nnon-adjacent pair of the complete set before the first band is cut,\nwith a padded box prefilter, and refuses a meet or a crossing by name:\nboth guides and the crossing point. The adjacent law stays in the band\nloop, unchanged.\n\nFixes #4032\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
